about='''<div class="wrap"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>It started with Bitcoin.</h1><p class="lede">I found crypto at 12 while looking for a way to get paid. Eventually, that led me to building Estate Protocol.</p></header><div class="about-grid"><div class="about-copy"><h2>The short version</h2><p>At 12, I made Zynga Poker’s national leaderboard, and people started asking to buy in-game chips for real money. I was too young to open a bank account, so I went looking for another way to get paid and found Bitcoin.</p><p>I sold chips for BTC, then sold the BTC for cash through P2P marketplaces like LocalBitcoins. Later, I traded the price differences between Indian and international crypto markets and wrote about security token offerings for WazirX.</p><h2>Building Estate</h2><p>With Estate Protocol, I brought together property inventory, a tokenization platform on Arbitrum, and the legal structure needed to distribute the offerings. I personally closed the partnerships and worked across product, compliance, fundraising, and integrations.</p><p>We originated $13M in property supply and listed 26+ properties. About 300 investors funded purchases. I raised $550K in investment capital and secured a separate $100K Arbitrum Foundation grant.</p><p>I led 14 people over the company’s history, with up to 11 working together at once. I also served as a judge and mentor for Arbitrum Founder House programs in Bengaluru and New York City.</p><h2>Outside work</h2><p>I read widely, still enjoy a game with asymmetric information, and spend a lot of time following the people and ideas shaping tokenization, DeFi, and stablecoins.</p></div><aside class="about-aside"><img src="assets/portrait.webp" alt="Parv Prabhakar" width="465" height="620"><div class="recognition"><p class="eyebrow">Along the way</p><div class="item"><strong>O-1A petition approved</strong>Recognition for extraordinary ability.</div><div class="item"><strong>Arbitrum Founder House</strong>Judge & mentor · Bengaluru and NYC.</div><div class="item"><strong>$100K Arbitrum grant</strong>Received after an initial rejection.</div></div></aside></div><section class="section"><div class="section-top"><h2>Speaking & press</h2><span class="eyebrow">Conversations about onchain finance</span></div><div class="photo-grid">'''
